      "content": "Utilizing high concentrations of essential oils, especially in medicine applications, can be extremely dangerous without medical training. Burns damage the skin's protective barrier and can cause a higher susceptibility to infection and other complications. Additionally, even if tea tree oil has some antimicrobial properties, it does not equate to medical-grade treatment. Commercial antiseptic solutions are specifically formulated to be used for wounds and have gone through significant safety and efficacy testing. It's also worth noting that a professional medical evaluation can prevent long-term damage and complications, which makes the visit worthwhile. The perceived self-sufficiency from managing it at home with essential oils overlooks potential risks such as allergic reactions, over-saturation, or incorrect dosage leading to worsened symptoms. Your health and safety are absolutely critical, and I would strongly advise against using such remedies on serious burns.",
